# Day 52 - 
# Python Built-in Functions

| Function | Use |
|----------|-----|
| print() | Displays output on the screen. |
| input() | Accepts input from the user. |
| len() | Returns the number of items in an object. |
| type() | Returns the data type of an object. |
| id() | Returns the unique identity (memory reference) of an object. |
| int() | Converts a value to an integer. |
| float() | Converts a value to a floating-point number. |
| str() | Converts a value to a string. |
| bool() | Converts a value to a Boolean (`True` or `False`). |
| list() | Creates a list or converts an iterable into a list. |
| tuple() | Creates a tuple or converts an iterable into a tuple. |
| set() | Creates a set and removes duplicate elements. |
| dict() | Creates a dictionary. |
| range() | Generates a sequence of numbers. |
| enumerate() | Returns both the index and value while iterating. |
| zip() | Combines elements from multiple iterables into tuples. |
| sorted() | Returns a new sorted list without modifying the original. |
| reversed() | Returns an iterator that accesses elements in reverse order. |
| sum() | Returns the sum of all elements in an iterable. |
| max() | Returns the largest element. |
| min() | Returns the smallest element. |
| abs() | Returns the absolute (positive) value of a number. |
| round() | Rounds a number to the specified number of decimal places. |
| pow() | Raises a number to a specified power. |
| divmod() | Returns the quotient and remainder as a tuple. |
| any() | Returns `True` if at least one element is `True`. |
| all() | Returns `True` if all elements are `True`. |
| chr() | Converts an ASCII/Unicode value to its corresponding character. |
| ord() | Returns the ASCII/Unicode value of a character. |
| bin() | Converts an integer to binary representation. |
| oct() | Converts an integer to octal representation. |
| hex() | Converts an integer to hexadecimal representation. |
| format() | Formats a value according to a specified format. |
| isinstance() | Checks whether an object belongs to a specified data type. |
| callable() | Checks whether an object can be called like a function. |
| dir() | Lists all attributes and methods of an object or module. |
| help() | Displays the documentation for an object, function, or module. |
| globals() | Returns a dictionary containing global variables. |
| locals() | Returns a dictionary containing local variables. |
| eval() | Evaluates a Python expression from a string. |
| exec() | Executes dynamically generated Python code. |

# Python String Methods


| String Method    | Use                                                                                     |
| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `capitalize()`   | Converts the first character to uppercase and the remaining characters to lowercase.    |
| `casefold()`     | Converts the entire string to lowercase for case-insensitive comparisons.               |
| `center()`       | Centers the string within a specified width by adding padding.                          |
| `count()`        | Counts the number of occurrences of a specified substring.                              |
| `encode()`       | Converts the string into bytes using the specified encoding.                            |
| `endswith()`     | Checks whether the string ends with a specified suffix.                                 |
| `expandtabs()`   | Replaces tab characters (`\t`) with spaces.                                             |
| `find()`         | Returns the index of the first occurrence of a substring, or `-1` if not found.         |
| `format()`       | Formats a string by inserting specified values.                                         |
| `format_map()`   | Formats a string using a mapping (dictionary).                                          |
| `index()`        | Returns the index of the first occurrence of a substring; raises an error if not found. |
| `isalnum()`      | Checks whether all characters are alphanumeric.                                         |
| `isalpha()`      | Checks whether all characters are alphabetic.                                           |
| `isascii()`      | Checks whether all characters are ASCII characters.                                     |
| `isdecimal()`    | Checks whether all characters are decimal digits.                                       |
| `isdigit()`      | Checks whether all characters are digits.                                               |
| `isidentifier()` | Checks whether the string is a valid Python identifier.                                 |
| `islower()`      | Checks whether all alphabetic characters are lowercase.                                 |
| `isnumeric()`    | Checks whether all characters are numeric.                                              |
| `isprintable()`  | Checks whether all characters are printable.                                            |
| `isspace()`      | Checks whether the string contains only whitespace characters.                          |
| `istitle()`      | Checks whether the string follows title case.                                           |
| `isupper()`      | Checks whether all alphabetic characters are uppercase.                                 |
| `join()`         | Joins the elements of an iterable into a single string using the specified separator.   |
| `ljust()`        | Left-aligns the string within a specified width.                                        |
| `lower()`        | Converts all characters to lowercase.                                                   |
| `lstrip()`       | Removes leading whitespace or specified characters.                                     |
| `maketrans()`    | Creates a translation table for use with `translate()`.                                 |
| `partition()`    | Splits the string into three parts using the first occurrence of a separator.           |
| `removeprefix()` | Removes the specified prefix if it exists.                                              |
| `removesuffix()` | Removes the specified suffix if it exists.                                              |
| `replace()`      | Replaces occurrences of a substring with another substring.                             |
| `rfind()`        | Returns the index of the last occurrence of a substring, or `-1` if not found.          |
| `rindex()`       | Returns the index of the last occurrence of a substring; raises an error if not found.  |
| `rjust()`        | Right-aligns the string within a specified width.                                       |
| `rpartition()`   | Splits the string into three parts using the last occurrence of a separator.            |
| `rsplit()`       | Splits the string from the right side.                                                  |
| `rstrip()`       | Removes trailing whitespace or specified characters.                                    |
| `split()`        | Splits the string into a list using a separator.                                        |
| `splitlines()`   | Splits the string into a list of lines.                                                 |
| `startswith()`   | Checks whether the string starts with a specified prefix.                               |
| `strip()`        | Removes leading and trailing whitespace or specified characters.                        |
| `swapcase()`     | Converts uppercase letters to lowercase and lowercase letters to uppercase.             |
| `title()`        | Converts the first character of each word to uppercase.                                 |
| `translate()`    | Replaces characters according to a translation table.                                   |
| `upper()`        | Converts all characters to uppercase.                                                   |
| `zfill()`        | Pads the string on the left with zeros until it reaches the specified length.           |









